- Blocker #5 (concurrent `--add-video` race) — would need `add_source_working.lock` plumbing
- Blocker #7 (disputed index-collision) — low reality
- Consider: URL normalization (youtu.be vs youtube.com/watch?v=), `Strategy -1` naming, help-text "skips silently" claim, local `import math` placement

Parallel-agent dispatch again proved fast and conflict-free despite all three editing the same file — Edit's file-modified guard caught the one near-collision and the agent re-read + re-applied cleanly.

## 10. [2026-04-18] Third parallel-agent sweep + polish: TSV defense, concurrent lock, URL canonicalization, polish

Final pass on the owls council findings from #8. Three parallel agents plus a quick inline polish wrap-up.

Prompts:
- "keep going"
- "ok, go ahead"

### 10a. TSV injection defense (blocker #3)
Added `_sanitize_tsv_field(s)` — strips `\t` → space, drops `\n` and `\r`. Applied inside `format_index_entry_line` to `title` and `source` before quoting/padding. `url` and `date` unaffected. Verified: round-trip of `'tab\there\nnewline\rcarriage'` emits a clean single-row TSV with no column corruption.

### 10b. Concurrent `--add-video` lock (blocker #5)
Added `_exclusive_file_lock(lock_path)` at module scope — `fcntl.flock(LOCK_EX)` context manager (blocking acquire, auto-release on exit/exception). Wrapped the entire critical section of `add_single_video()` — from the max_idx_f scan through tracking-file writes — with the lock on `add_source_working.lock`. Coexists correctly with the existing `claim_index`/`release_index` per-video locks used by the multi-session resume path.

Tradeoff: lock is held across whisper fallback (potentially minutes for long videos on CPU whisper). Accepted the pessimistic-but-bulletproof variant per spec; could be tightened later if contention becomes an issue.

### 10c. URL canonicalization (consider item)
New `normalize_youtube_url(url)` helper (lines 107-160) uses `urllib.parse.urlparse`/`parse_qs` to canonicalize any recognized YouTube URL variant to `https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=<ID>`:
- `www.youtube.com/watch?v=X` + `list=…&index=…` tail → stripped to bare `watch?v=X`
- `youtube.com`, `m.youtube.com`, `youtu.be/X`, `/shorts/X` — all canonicalized
- Schemeless URLs handled (prepends `https://` before parsing)
- Non-YouTube input returned unchanged (never raises)

Wired into two dedup sites:
- `_match_sources_by_title` Strategy `"native-url"` — builds `{normalize(u): original_u}` map, normalizes each `source.url` for comparison, returns original index.list URL on match
- `add_single_video` duplicate check — pre-canonicalizes the `ok_urls ∪ v2t_urls ∪ existing_urls` set and checks `normalize(video_url)` membership; prints canonical form in the skip message when the user-given form differed

### 10d. Inline polish (4 items)
Did these myself after agents returned, since they're each one-liners:
- `import math` hoisted from `add_single_video` function-body to module top (next to `import unicodedata`)
- `Strategy -1` comments at two sites → `Strategy "native-url"` (descriptive, no magic number)
- Help text for `--add-video`: "Skips silently" → "Skips (with a message)" + adds note about canonical-form matching
- Clean-up the deferred URL-normalization wiring in `add_single_video` (agent 3 intentionally left this off-limits to avoid colliding with agent 2's lock wrap)

### 10e. Owls tally — final

| Item | State |
|------|-------|
| Blocker #1 data loss in reindex | ✓ |
| Blocker #2 needless rewrites | ✓ |
| Blocker #3 TSV injection | ✓ |
